# SGOT Project Overview

SGOT is an internal web application for managing work orders, technical scheduling, and warehouse outputs for a security/electronics company.

## Purpose

SGOT complements existing physical documents and SIIGO.

It does NOT replace:
- SIIGO inventory
- quotations
- billing
- supplier management
- physical work orders
- physical warehouse output documents

## Main roles

- Administrador / Almacén
- Comercial
- Jefe Técnica
- Gerencia

Technicians do not log into SGOT in V1.

## Responsibilities

### Administrador / Almacén
- Registers work orders received physically.
- Selects the commercial advisor associated with the work order.
- Manages customers, products, technicians and work types.
- Creates warehouse outputs.
- Registers delivered and returned materials.
- Handles operational workflow.

### Comercial
- Does NOT create work orders in SGOT.
- Can view only their own work orders.
- Can monitor status, assigned technician and scheduling information.

### Jefe Técnica
- Can view work orders.
- Can assign/reassign technician and scheduled date.
- Must not have unrestricted permission to edit the entire work order.

### Gerencia
- Read-only access to operational information and future dashboards.

## Work order workflow

Valid statuses:

1. RECEIVED
2. PENDING_EQUIPMENT
3. EQUIPMENT_OK
4. IN_INSTALLATION
5. COMPLETED

Do not invent additional statuses unless explicitly requested.

## Important business rules

- A physical OT already exists before SGOT registration.
- Warehouse registers the OT after receiving it.
- One OT can contain multiple products/equipment.
- One OT can require multiple installation visits but remains the same OT.
- One OT can have at most one WarehouseOutput.
- Original requested quantities must remain available for traceability.
- Warehouse used quantity is calculated as delivered quantity minus returned quantity.
- Products/materials not originally included in the OT may appear in the warehouse output.
- SIIGO remains the inventory and billing source of truth.